      "page_idx": 28,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.367,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.089,
            0.729,
            0.113
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3.7 Addition and Subtraction of Decimals"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.121,
            0.848,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": "？ Priya requires 2.7 m of cloth for her skirt, and Shylaja requires 3.5m for her kurti. What is the total quantity of cloth needed?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.171,
            0.574,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": "We have to find the sum of $2.7 m  + 3.5 m$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.194,
            0.848,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": "Earlier, we saw how to add $2   \\frac { 7 } { 1 0 } \\pm   3   \\frac { 5 } { 1 0 }$ (also shown below). Can you carry out the same addition using decimal notation? It is shown below. Share your observations."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.274,
            0.577,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "The total quantity of cloth needed is 6.2 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.313,
            0.681,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\begin{array}{r}2 \\quad \\frac{7}{10} \\\\+ 3 \\quad \\frac{5}{10} \\\\\\end{array}}{\\begin{array}{r}= \\quad 5 \\quad \\frac{12}{10} \\\\\\end{array}} \\\\= \\quad 6 \\quad \\frac{2}{10}\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_28_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.504,
            0.713,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "How much longer is Shylaja’s cloth compared to Priya’s?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.544,
            0.847,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "We have to find the difference of 3.5m – 2.7m. Again, observe how the differences $3\\frac{5}{10} \\sim 2\\frac{7}{10}$ and $3.5m = 2.7m$ are computed."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.616,
            0.44,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{ccc}3\\quad \\dfrac{5}{10} & \\longrightarrow \\quad 2\\quad \\dfrac{15}{10} \\\\\\dfrac{-2\\quad \\dfrac{7}{10}}{} & \\longrightarrow \\quad \\dfrac{-2\\quad \\dfrac{7}{10}}{} \\\\\\hline& \\longrightarrow \\quad \\dfrac{8}{10} \\\\\\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_28_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.565,
            0.607,
            0.801,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array} { r l r } { { 3 . 5 } } & { { } \\longrightarrow } & { \\stackrel { 2 } { 2 . 5 } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } & { { } } \\end{array} \\quad \\begin{array} { r l } { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } \\\\ { { } } & { { } } \\end{array} \\quad .",
          "image_source": "images/page_28_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.751,
            0.848,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": "As you can see, the standard procedure for adding and subtracting whole numbers can be used to add and subtract decimals."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.788,
            0.848,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": "A detailed view of the underlying place value calculation is shown below for the sum 75.345 + 86.691. Its compact form is shown next to it."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
